// Package sample is a golden fixture: a `return` inside a function literal
// inside the operand of another `return`, so that one probe site encloses
// another and the inner rewrite is folded into the outer one's operand before
// that operand is folded onto a line.
package sample

// Nested totals two numbers through a literal, so that the outer return's
// first operand holds a return of its own.
//
// The two rewrites want temporaries of the same name, and the literal is where
// that has to be harmless: a declared name's scope begins at the end of its own
// specification, so the outer temporary is not in scope inside its own
// initialiser, and the inner block declares one of its own in any case.
func Nested(a, b int) (int, error) {
	return func() int {
		return a + b
	}(), nil
}
